<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Anshi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Anshi was a Chinese statesman and chancellor of the Northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> in the eleventh century. He introduced a sweeping programme of reforms, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-policies-song">New Policies</a>, including state loans to farmers, changes to taxation and labour service, and reorganisation of the militia. The Song Dynasty profile treats his reforms as a major and divisive episode in Song economic and political history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wang-anshi.jpg" alt="Wang Anshi" width="313" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wang_Anshi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
